# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.local

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
# `.vscode/*` rather than `.vscode/`, so the negation below can take effect — git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, and a re-include under one is silently ignored.
.vscode/*
# ...but DO share settings.json. It is not a personal preference file here: this workspace's root holds ~400 GB
# of simulation output (runs/ alone is 310 GB), and VS Code's file watcher does NOT read .gitignore, so every
# clone re-registers recursive watches over it — handles and CPU on Windows, exhausted inotify watches on
# Linux. Leaving each contributor to rediscover that is not an editor preference, it is a setup defect.
!.vscode/settings.json

# Model output — full simOut + ParCa cache stay LOCAL (huge; license-restricted). Never commit.
runs/
# comparison / scratch output roots (runs_native, runs_codeonly, ...). .gitignore has no inline
# comments, so these must sit on their own lines. manifest.py's _NORM_PATH already treats
# `runs_<suffix>` as a run root, so the naming is not new here.
runs_*/
out/

# Do NOT ignore data/cache — the cached demo results are committed for reproducibility.
# EXCEPT these raw-run reader caches: regenerated on the fly when reading raw simOut, local-only, not needed by
# the committed-shard read path (the test suite is green without them):
data/cache/variant_map.json
data/cache/gene_map.json
src/cellarium/_pathway_resolved.json
# NOTE: data/cache/gene_scope.json IS committed (NOT ignored). It is model-derived but NOT regenerable without
# Docker + sim_data, and the KO/launch path (gene symbol -> ko_index) needs it — a fresh clone must ship with it,
# or test_launch reddens and no knockout can be proposed. The C3 staleness guard (scope.cache_status) rebuilds it
# only if the model is later recompiled locally.
# Manifest shards (data/manifest/*.parquet) ARE committed — they are the shareable corpus.

# The whole paper/ tree is out of the distributed repo: it holds blind-review drafts and
# manuscripts that are not part of the software artifact.
paper/
# scratch campaign scripts
scratchpad_campaign.py*

# local durable chat sessions (user data)
data/sessions.db

# SCI-1: the iML1515 SBML (~11 MB) is fetched on demand from BiGG (fba.fetch_model()), not committed
data/fba/

# SCI-2: PRECISE-1K RNA-seq (~60 MB counts) is fetched on demand (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.8284223), not committed
data/precise1k/
data/evidence.jsonl

# CI: pytest JUnit report (written by the failing-test annotator step)
pytest-report.xml
vendor/wcEcoliRelease-v3.0.1.tar.gz


# BACKLOG.md is local working state, not part of the distributed artifact.
# src/cellarium/harness.py recreates it (section X) on first use in a fresh clone.
BACKLOG.md

# The HF upload ledger is a hand-maintained record of ONE contributor's uploads (paths, sizes, what is still
# local-only). Nothing generates it, so it is not a feature a cloner inherits — it is personal bookkeeping.
data/hf/UPLOAD_LEDGER.md

# Generated sweep outputs. scripts/refit_sweep.py writes refit_sweep/ (OUT = "refit_sweep"),
# 2.7 GB across 28 pseudo_*_RNA trees; parca4_work/ holds its ParCa inputs. Both regenerate,
# and neither belongs in a clone. They were previously excluded only at the editor level
# (.vscode/settings.json), which does not stop `git add -A` from staging them.
refit_sweep/
parca4_work/

# Records ONE contributor's HF uploads by repo id and local path, written when raw run
# directories were deleted to reclaim disk. It is the key for restoring them, so it stays
# local, but it names a personal HF repo and must never be committed.
data/hf_reclaim_manifest.json

# Design-history and planning notes. Both are cited by code and docs as plain-text
# references (no markdown links, no runtime reads), and HYPOTHESIS_MODE_PLAN.md carries
# Status/Owners headers naming people. Appendix "Reproducibility and scope" commits the
# distributed supplement to carrying no planning notes, so they stay local.
docs/ROADMAP.md
docs/HYPOTHESIS_MODE_PLAN.md

# The raw GEO record. NCBI asks that records be retrieved from GEO rather than redistributed, and
# the paper's asset register commits to that, so scripts/gse2065_reanalysis.py fetches it on demand
# and checks it against a pinned SHA-256. The DERIVED tables beside it are committed.
data/gse2065/GSE2065_family.soft.gz

# anonymous.4open.science serves NO image format. Probed against the live mirror: .pdf, .svg, .png and
# .jpg all return {"error":"file_not_supported"} — and they do so for paths that do not exist, while
# .csv and .txt return file_not_found, so the check is on the extension, not the file. A committed
# figure in any image format is therefore simply absent from the artifact a reviewer downloads.
# `--plot` regenerates both locally in about a second, which is the honest place for it to live.
data/gse2065/figure1_panels_bc.pdf
data/gse2065/figure1_panels_bc.svg
